# BL-1102: 286 -> 99 *, 180 -> 66 validator, 10 -> 9 inproc. The validator no longer fires R13's self-probe (its 23 traced
# removals over a probe world) or M1's, so c-write is a one-receipt traced run like the others, the m1 and
# c-restricted-seeds starts are gone, and the probe-world build is gone from the in-process passes. Measured by one counted
# run through core/scripts/hermetic-run.sh (the judge's own J3 output) at this change's tip; the push's counted run is the
# second.
# BL-899 enumeration removal: 99 -> 111 *, 66 -> 73 validator. The new cell c-enum-unguarded is one start, one --score-one
# and three --r13-one workers (two named removals and the enumeration removal); pop-1 gains one --r13-one (world e's
# enumeration removal); c-committed's world follows DEFAULT_MAX_R13 (5 -> 6), so it gains one --r13-one and that removal's
# seeded receipt run. The rest of * is the seeded receipts those removals run. Measured the same way.
# Every distinct state is ONE FXCELL-tagged cli start of a validator copy (21 cells, cells.decl), its workers covered by
# the one self-nested row. c-m1-e2e and cli-wire drive real --score-one and --r13-one workers.
# inproc 9: untraced_fn 3 (one per r13_untraced call) and base_setup 3 per pass (vbr_sec_env, vbr_sec_args,
# vbr_sec_setup) x 2 passes = 6; every in-process call is paired with its own fx_inproc (arm P2).
105 *
70 scripts/validate-backlog-receipts.sh
9 inproc:scripts/validate-backlog-receipts.sh
